  "reason": "Evidence: scvi_n200 singleprofile (config_004, acc=0.5203) is the best configuration so far, clearly outperforming pca_n2000 (0.4849) and scgpt (0.4106) among RNA encoders, and vastly outperforming image-only resnet50 (0.2079). The multiprofile dimension is completely untested for any encoder. Question: Does moving from singleprofile to multiprofile with simple avgpool aggregation improve upon the best single-profile scvi_n200 result? This isolates the effect of profile setting/aggregation on the strongest encoder. Why this is best: It is the most natural exploitation of the current best result (scvi_n200) along the most important untested axis (multiprofile). Using avgpool keeps the experiment simple, avoiding confounding from a more complex transformer aggregator. If multiprofile+avgpool helps, config_006 (transformer) becomes a logical follow-up; if it doesn't, we can pivot to multimodal or image-encoder exploration with the remaining 5 experiments. This maximizes information gain per experiment under the tight budget."
}

